  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rahumathullah (M/58) vs Dean on 25 August, 2021 Author: Senthilkumar Ramamoorthy Bench: Senthilkumar Ramamoorthy W.P(Md)N Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 25.08.2021 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice Senthilkumar Ramamoorthy W.P(MD)No.15046 of 2021 Rahumathullah (M/58), S/o. Kamalutheen, 15/5/12, NondiKaattubava Lane, Thiruppathur, Sivagangai District. ... Vs. 1. Dean, Government Medical College Hospital, Ramanathapuram. 2. M.R.Kannan .. Prayer : Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of In praying this Court to issue a Writ of Mandamus directing to the first re to consider the petitioner's tender for providing perishable food for th respondent's hospital from 01.07.2021 to till 31.12.2021 by considering representation dated 30.06.2021. For Petitioner : Mr. P. Venkata Subramanian For Respondents : Mr.R.Baskaran, Counsel for State https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis/ Rahumathullah (M/58) vs Dean on 25 August, 2021",
    "facts": "The petitioner seeks the consideration and disposal of his representation dated 30.06.2021 to the first respondent in relation to the tender submitted by him for a contract for the provision of perishable food products. 2. The petitioner states that he is a food supply contractor. The first respondent had floated a tender for the supply of perishable food products. The petitioner had submitted a bid by duly enclosing all relevant documents. Contrary to the petitioner's expectations, it is stated that the contract was awarded to the second respondent herein. The petitioner alleges that the successful tenderer does not have a registration from the Food Safety and Standard Authority of India (FSSAI). In such circumstances, the petitioner submitted the representation and seeks the consideration thereof.",
